{"id":"expl:packages/core/src/working-overlay.ts@L103","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/core/src/working-overlay.ts","span":{"start":103,"end":103}},"file":"packages/core/src/working-overlay.ts","span":{"start":103,"end":103},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:f6932cf0b44bc76addef40cc101483db13750719f6591db5c54692a194fa604a","meta":{"text":"The canonical-manifest fingerprint captured at seed/resync time (for drift comparison)."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/core/src/working-overlay.ts@L108","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/core/src/working-overlay.ts","span":{"start":108,"end":113}},"file":"packages/core/src/working-overlay.ts","span":{"start":108,"end":113},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:ef87b380698c7c4957675cbe6263634eeebb9d8ef6f68b24ebb9229735769689","meta":{"text":"Has the canonical ON-DISK soul advanced since the overlay last seeded? An external `crib update`\n(or `crib index`) bumps `generation.extracted` + `lastUpdated` + usually `vcsHead`; this returns\ntrue when any of those moved, so the watch fallback knows to {@link resync} before refreshing.\nCheap: one `readFileSync` of the graph manifest, no graph hydration."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/core/src/working-overlay.ts@L126","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/core/src/working-overlay.ts","span":{"start":126,"end":134}},"file":"packages/core/src/working-overlay.ts","span":{"start":126,"end":134},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:41ada2c537a70adc4b7dfa72d5331619d53e35eceb864fbb4fafa1c841715d96","meta":{"text":"Mark a file dirty: record it for re-parse on the next refresh. Does NOT drop the overlay's records\nyet — the reverse-dependency closure is computed from the CANONICAL soul (whose edges are always\nintact) inside the pipeline refresher BEFORE removal, mirroring `updateRepo`'s closure-before-\nremove ordering. If we removed here, the incoming `B→dirty` edges would vanish from the overlay and\nthe closure scan would miss B, silently dropping the edge (the P0-1 fix from `updateRepo`). Until\nthe next refresh, reads see the pre-edit overlay state for this file — the freshness window is one\ndebounce. Idempotent."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/core/src/working-overlay.ts@L139","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/core/src/working-overlay.ts","span":{"start":139,"end":144}},"file":"packages/core/src/working-overlay.ts","span":{"start":139,"end":144},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:c78f01d438b148acd5c3cd382f4617b7a088c27d94e30790d054a710e5fca706","meta":{"text":"Cold-path re-seed: re-hydrate the overlay from the canonical ON-DISK soul (picking up an external\n`crib update`) and clear the dirty set. The caller then re-marks the still-dirty files from VCS\n(`uncommittedChanges` ∪ `untrackedFiles`) and calls the pipeline refresher to re-parse them. O(the\ncanonical graph) but infrequent — only on detected drift or restart."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/core/src/working-overlay.ts@L151","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/core/src/working-overlay.ts","span":{"start":151,"end":157}},"file":"packages/core/src/working-overlay.ts","span":{"start":151,"end":157},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:c6a3fab14618f2352ad76bd2afee5617b27a6aee251ecb42c8cae02b9e867c31","meta":{"text":"Restore a SINGLE committed file into the overlay (used when a file leaves the dirty set without a\nfull resync — e.g. the watch refresh path determined a file is byte-identical to canonical and can\ndrop out of the overlay). Copies the canonical node/edge records for `path` from `canonical` back\ninto the overlay store after removing the overlay's current records for that path. Edges whose\nOTHER endpoint is also dirty are skipped — the dirty endpoint's re-parse will re-emit them."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/core/src/working-overlay.ts@L37","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/core/src/working-overlay.ts","span":{"start":37,"end":37}},"file":"packages/core/src/working-overlay.ts","span":{"start":37,"end":37},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:256b4fbd36427647361e929a6dcbc9f09cdf4af3d96fb851639ba50c736e3984","meta":{"text":"The canonical-manifest fields the overlay watches for drift caused by an external `crib update`."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/core/src/working-overlay.ts@L46","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/core/src/working-overlay.ts","span":{"start":46,"end":52}},"file":"packages/core/src/working-overlay.ts","span":{"start":46,"end":52},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:ac071188f6072f96e74361f1ac2a4d166f6010272b5d0423965798b05d0bfb4b","meta":{"text":"Read the ON-DISK canonical graph manifest (not an in-memory SoulStore's possibly-stale copy) so the\nwatch fallback can detect that another process advanced the committed soul. Reads `.crib/graph/\nmanifest.json` — the FULL graph manifest that carries `stats`/`generation`/`repo.vcsHead` — NOT the\nbyte-stable `.crib/crib.json` bootstrap locator, which strips those fields and would never show\ndrift. Returns `null` when the manifest is absent (un-indexed — the overlay wouldn't be active)."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/core/src/working-overlay.ts@L71","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/core/src/working-overlay.ts","span":{"start":71,"end":71}},"file":"packages/core/src/working-overlay.ts","span":{"start":71,"end":71},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:26f998cc02956be3f8fb08f51234198acaf3aec5de301026618b12294b9489f9","meta":{"text":"The ephemeral in-memory store that holds canonical + the dirty swap. Never persisted."}}
